# AI Idea Validator — environment variables
#
# Names are namespaced to this app on purpose. Generic names like
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL collide across the ~95 repos in
# Projects/ — a shared Upstash database in particular would let one project's
# traffic eat another's rate-limit budget.
#
# Local dev:  copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.
# Production: set these in Netlify → Site settings → Environment variables.

# ── Required: the analysis model ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic API key. Each submission runs Claude Opus 5 twice — a web-search
# research call, then the analysis — so this key carries real per-run cost.
# Create one at https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys
IDEA_VALIDATOR_ANTHROPIC_KEY=

# ── Required: rate limiting ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Upstash Redis, backing a sliding-window limiter (3/min and 25/day per IP).
#
# The route FAILS CLOSED without these — it returns 503 rather than running an
# uncapped premium-model endpoint. That is deliberate: an unavailable validator
# is recoverable, an unmetered one is not.
#
# Create a database at https://console.upstash.com/redis — use a NEW database
# for this app, not one shared with another project. Both values are on the
# database's "REST API" tab.
IDEA_VALIDATOR_UPSTASH_URL=
IDEA_VALIDATOR_UPSTASH_TOKEN=

# ── No longer used ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPENAI_API_KEY — the analysis moved from gpt-4o-mini to Claude Opus 5.
# Safe to delete from Netlify once this deploy is live.
